  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement is partly resolved by the native supplement: the measure, finite-interval normalization, and Bochner integral are adequately identified. The direct judgment's explicit maximum-coordinate norm identification remains unsupported by the supplied expansions. The final classification remains undetermined because that triggered dependency question is not fully resolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D042–D044 delegate their norm fields to unexpanded Pi.seminormedAddGroup and Pi.seminormedRing. The supplement explicitly states that the bridge probe's norm outputs are not supplied."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The request is justified as an evidence question rather than an established mathematical mismatch. Inspecting the supplement resolves the measure and integral objections, but does not fully resolve the norm objection.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native spans include Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id, Real.volume_Ioc, MeasureTheory.integral_def, the L1 construction, and a finite-vector integral_eq specialization; they omit the additional norm outputs."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined with a narrower basis. The unresolved measure and integral meanings in the blind packet are no longer outstanding after supplement inspection. Exact product-norm identification and reconciliation remain outstanding.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation flags D042, D043, D044, D061, D091, and D101. The supplement supplies operative characterizations for the last three, but no coordinate characterization of the first three."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D042 unclear",
      "resolution": "D042 constructs a normed additive commutative group on finite real coordinate vectors, retaining the norm and pseudometric from Pi.seminormedAddGroup. Its bundled normed-group status is established, but the exact inherited coordinate formula is not exposed. This uncertainty remains.",
      "primary_evidence": "D042 explicitly sets toNorm := __src.toNorm and toPseudoMetricSpace := __src.toPseudoMetricSpace with __src := Pi.seminormedAddGroup."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D043 unclear",
      "resolution": "D043 uses the same named underlying product seminormed-group construction as D042 and supplies the normed-group interface used for integrability. The supplied bodies support that structural relationship, but do not expose the underlying norm formula.",
      "primary_evidence": "D043 inherits toNorm, toAddGroup, and toPseudoMetricSpace from Pi.seminormedAddGroup; the target uses this instance through NormedAddGroup.toENormedAddMonoid in all four IntervalIntegrable premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D044 unclear",
      "resolution": "D044 fixes the norm used consistently in all four error inequalities. Its norm comes from Pi.seminormedRing, whose body is absent. The direct judge's assertion that this is the maximum absolute component is not independently established by the permitted declaration evidence. A norm mismatch is not demonstrated.",
      "primary_evidence": "D044 sets toNorm := __src.toNorm for __src := Pi.seminormedRing. The fully explicit target selects NormedRing.toNorm of this instance for every error magnitude."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D061 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved. The selected real volume is ordinary length measure on the real Borel space, rather than an arbitrary or rescaled measure.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native supplement expands Real.measureSpace through measureSpaceOfInnerProductSpace, identifies its measurable space with borel ℝ, and supplies Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id and Real.volume_Ioc : volume (Set.Ioc a b) = ENNReal.ofReal (b - a)."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D091 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved on the target's effective domain. The real conversions of the two interval measures equal their strictly positive lengths. Conversion at infinity is therefore irrelevant here; its general behavior need not be inferred from the unexpanded toNNReal.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement defines Measure.real μ S = (μ S).toReal and supplies Real.volume_real_Ioc_of_le. The target assumes a < b and s < t."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D101 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved for this target. The integral is Bochner integration obtained from L1 integration, with explicit default branches outside integrability or completeness. The finite-real-vector specialization and four integrability premises avoid those defaults; the difference of the two integrable face histories is integrable as well.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement gives integral_def, integral_eq, Integrable.coeFn_toL1, the continuous extension from simple-function integration, and the native specialization of integral_eq to α → Fin m → ℝ."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The average-related completeness objection is resolved. Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation, the statement contains the local update and conditional propagation of the three independent errors. It does not establish conservation for arbitrary q, construct an accurate rule, or prove the separate discontinuity assertions. The physical law appropriately remains inherited context for this local calculation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5 defines volume-normalized averages and edge-flux updates. D001–D004 and the target supply four normalized averages, the update, a weighted error identity, and the conditional estimate. Q7 explicitly selects independent old-average and time-averaged physical-flux bounds."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The local operators, restricted measure, interval orientation, normalization, and integral construction are resolved. C06 remains partially unresolved solely because D042–D044 do not expose the exact inherited norm and its reconciliation across the analytic instances.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001–D004 give the complete local definition bodies; D079 defines the oriented integral; the supplement supplies restriction and Bochner characterizations. D042–D044 retain unexpanded norm projections."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved for the displayed local premises. Positive finite interval measures exclude exceptional normalization, and positive lengths exclude zero division. No differentiability is required. The endpoint fluxes are the actual supplied compositions flux(q(a,τ)) and flux(q(b,τ)); neither half-open integration nor the inherited receipt proves their suitability for every representative of a discontinuous solution.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes a < b, s < t, four local integrability conditions, and balance for precisely those endpoint compositions. Printed pages 4–5 retain integral conservation at discontinuities without specifying traces. The inherited receipt prohibits enlargement into a pointwise representative convention."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target consistently uses one selected norm in its error inequalities, and Q7 permits a norm-based realization without attributing that norm to the book. Triangle inequality and real homogeneity suffice for the algebraic estimate, so no norm-specific counterexample is established. Nevertheless, the demanded identification of the selected norm and reconciliation with the integration instances remain incomplete.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target uses Pi.normedRing for every error norm. The native norm_le_of_weighted_error_balance declaration is generic over a real normed space. The packet omits the norm-characterization outputs."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under Q7 and the applicable inherited rectangle convention, the target structurally supplies the intended local conditional update claim, with physical and numerical quantities separate and the correct signs. Full certification remains unclear because the triggered exact norm identification is unresolved. No inference to global conservation or unconditional accuracy is made.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target gives U' = U - (Δt/Δx) • (G_R - G_L) and Δx • (U' - Q_t) = Δx • (U - Q_s) + Δt • ((G_L - F_L) - (G_R - F_R)); printed equation (1.10) fixes the corresponding physical left-minus-right sign."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Under Q7 and the applicable inherited rectangle convention, ordinary normalized rectangle conservation yields the displayed error identity, and compatible norm laws yield the bound. The measure and integral steps are now supported. Certification for the exact selected analytic instances remains unclear pending resolution of D042–D044; the printed paragraph alone does not supply the quantitative theorem.",
      "primary_evidence": "D004 normalizes by interval length, D003 defines the update, and hphysicalBalance gives the exact local reference balance. The native supplement confirms length measure and genuine finite-vector integrals, but omits the additional norm evidence."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, applicability, and purported strength",
      "resolution": "The physical premises are satisfiable, and the estimate permits nonzero numerical error. For m = 1, unit spatial and temporal intervals, zero physical state and flux, zero old numerical value, and numerical face outputs 0 and a nonzero vector v, the updated error is -v and the bound with rightBound = ‖v‖ is attained. Abstract labels impose no mesh or stencil restriction. The theorem assumes only one rectangle balance and does not require a globally conservative extension. These facts establish meaningful local applicability, not a basis for classifying the theorem as faithful-stronger.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target's binders allow Cell = Unit and Face = Bool, and D003 gives the stated nonzero update. The supplement's integral_const characterizes the zero physical integrals. The target has no global solution predicate or smoothness assumption."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the applicable inherited rectangle-conservation convention, the normalized averages, numerical-data dependence, signed update, and independent conditional error propagation match the selected local claim. The supplement resolves length measure, finite positive normalization, and genuine Bochner integration. However, the supplied evidence does not fully identify the exact norm inherited through D042–D044 or reconcile those instances as requested by the triggered review. Thus the complete implication remains uncertified, although no substantive norm mismatch is established. This comparison does not include proving the inherited physical law or any global or unconditional numerical claim."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the same recorded conventions, write h = b-a and k = t-s. The local physical balance gives h(Q_t-Q_s) = k(F_L-F_R). The defined numerical update then gives h(U'-Q_t) = h(U-Q_s) + k((G_L-F_L)-(G_R-F_R)); compatible norm homogeneity and triangle inequality yield the stated bound. The other conjuncts follow from positivity, integrability, and the supplied interval-volume characterizations. This establishes the intended mathematical derivation, but the exact norm-instance identification remains an unresolved evidence obligation. The printed source alone does not select this quantitative formulation."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The permitted evidence does not expand Pi.seminormedAddGroup and Pi.seminormedRing or provide an exact characterization connecting their norm fields in the target's finite-real-vector instances. The maximum absolute-component formula asserted by the direct judge is therefore not independently certified here.",
    "The printed passage leaves the discrete formula, norm, quantitative accuracy, and discontinuous endpoint interpretation unspecified. Q7 and the inherited receipt qualify this comparison within their recorded scopes; they do not remove those original source ambiguities."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "remaining-norm-evidence-gap",
      "evidence": "D042–D044 expose inherited norm projections rather than coordinate formulas. The supplement expressly omits the bridge probe's norm outputs. Its generic norm estimate and finite-vector integral specialization do not themselves supply the missing coordinate characterization.",
      "impact": "The exact norm dependency question remains unresolved. This prevents complete acceptance under the requested evidence-bound audit, without establishing that the theorem uses an incorrect norm."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "measure-and-integral-objections-resolved",
      "evidence": "The native supplement identifies real volume with the identity Stieltjes measure, gives interval volumes and their real conversions, and characterizes Bochner integration through L1 with an actual finite-real-vector specialization.",
      "impact": "D061, D091, and D101 no longer justify uncertainty on this target's effective domain. Reused hashes establish provenance; the supplied declarations establish the relevant mathematical meanings."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-and-representative-scope",
      "evidence": "Printed Section 1.2 is qualitative. Q7 separately selects conditional error propagation. The target assumes one rectangle balance using explicit endpoint compositions, while the inherited receipt supplies no unrestricted representative convention.",
      "impact": "Any later acceptance must remain interpretation-qualified and local. It cannot certify a printed quantitative theorem, arbitrary discontinuous representatives, global mesh conservation, or unconditional accuracy."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source renderings and the exact inline declaration, translation, judgment, and supplement evidence without tools or target-proof reasoning. I did not recompute source or rendering hashes. The mathematical local update and error identity have the correct normalization, signs, dependencies, and nonvacuous domain under the recorded conventions. The supplement resolves substantial blind-packet gaps, but the direct judgment overstates what the supplied evidence establishes about the explicit coordinate norm. Retaining a narrowly grounded undetermined classification preserves that remaining uncertainty rather than treating either judgment as authoritative."
}
